mproved Seals 3",[59]="Healing Light 1",[60]="Healing Light 2"},notes={[10]="Open with Redoubt: blocking pays off at once, and Shield Specialization needs all five ranks.",[15]="Precision and Anticipation help you land hits and dodge them while questing with a shield.",[20]="Improved Seal of Fury and Improved Righteous Fury begin the mana and mitigation cycle Forever tanking is built on.",[29]="Around 20 points in, you match the usual dungeon-tank setup: Shield Specialization, Sacred Duty and Swift Judgement are complete.",[33]="Templar's Bulwark is an absorb cooldown that scales with your health, and Holy Shield later in the plan requires it.",[37]="Iron Creed adds threat and damage reduction to Holy Strike while Righteous Fury is active.",[42]="Holy Shield is the capstone: more block uptime, with Holy damage each time you block. Ideal for pulling packs.",[43]="Leftover points buy armor, a quicker Hammer of Justice, and Holy Strength and seal damage for leveling."}},{key="retribution",spec="Retribution",split="10/0/41",link="https://foreverdb.net/class/Paladin/talents?lvl=60&t=055fe0.50203--55225331221331021",talents={[10]="Benediction 1",[11]="Benediction 2",[12]="Benediction 3",[13]="Benediction 4",[14]="Benediction 5",[15]="Improved Judgement 1",[16]="Improved Judgement 2",[17]="Conviction 1",[18]="Conviction 2",[19]="Conviction 3",[20]="Seal of Command 1",[21]="Sanctified Judgement 1",[22]="Sanctified Judgement 2",[23]="Sanctified Judgement 3",[24]="Conviction 4",[25]="Conviction 5",[26]="Vindication 1",[27]="Vindication 2",[28]="Vindication 3",[29]="Sacred Arbiter 1",[30]="Vengeance 1",[31]="Vengeance 2",[32]="Vengeance 3",[33]="Two-Handed Weapon Specialization 1",[34]="Two-Handed Weapon Specialization 2",[35]="Two-Handed Weapon Specialization 3",[36]="Pursuit of Justice 1",[37]="Pursuit of Justice 2",[38]="Holy Conduit 1",[39]="Holy Conduit 2",[40]="Twist of Light 1",[41]="Instrument of Law 1",[42]="Instrument of Law 2",[43]="Divine Strength 1",[44]="Divine Strength 2",[45]="Divine Strength 3",[46]="Divine Strength 4",[47]="Divine Strength 5",[48]="Improved Seals 1",[49]="Improved Seals 2",[50]="Improved Seals 3",[51]="Healing Light 1",[52]="Healing Light 2",[53]="Deflection 1",[54]="Deflection 2",[55]="Deflection 3",[56]="Deflection 4",[57]="Deflection 5",[58]="Repentance 1",[59]="Eye for an Eye 1",[60]="Eye for an Eye 2"},notes={[10]="Benediction lowers the mana cost of Judgement, Holy Strike and seals, so you rest less between fights.",[20]="Seal of Command is the main two-hander seal for leveling; take it as soon as it opens.",[21]="Sanctified Judgement gives mana back and is the prerequisite arrow for Vengeance.",[29]="Sacred Arbiter strengthens Holy Strike and keeps Judgements rolling, and completes the 20 points row 5 asks for.",[30]="Vengeance, then Two-Handed Weapon Specialization: the crit-driven damage core of the two-hander plan.",[36]="Pursuit of Justice adds run speed. Champion of the Light is left out while the Retribution Aura spell-power bug keeps spell damage low.",[40]="Twist of Light makes swapping seals cheaper and adds seal echoes; it is Forever's seal-twisting talent.",[43]="Spare points go to Divine Strength and Holy's Improved Seals for damage, then Deflection for survival."}}}})

